{:adr/id 345
 :adr/status :accepted
 :adr/date "2026-09-08"
 :decision :option-in-return-position-already-lowered-so-the-guard-is-the-deliverable

 :summary
 "kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang lang/compat.edn recorded, under
  :measured :option-return-on-wasm32, that a function returning an option with
  option-some on one arm of an `if` and option-none on the other compiled on
  KIR and REFUSED wasm32 and wasm32-browser -- and refused the WHOLE project
  even when main never reached it. Re-measured at amu 9092ee34 it lowers,
  RUNS, and answers, on all three targets. No compiler change was needed. The
  deliverable is therefore the guard that was missing, plus the correction of
  an authority that had been steering guest code for six days after the thing
  it described stopped being true."

 :re-measurement
 {:at "2026-09-08, amu 9092ee34cc32b53ca998c473f7172e2f172abd8b"
  :previously "2026-09-02, amu bb51dc14: exit 70, \"unsupported typed Wasm expression\""
  :single-module
  {:source "(defn- pick [n :i64] [:option :i64] (if (> n 0) (option-some-of [:option :i64] n) (option-none-of [:option :i64])))"
   :wasm32 {:exit 0 :ran 7}
   :wasm32-browser {:exit 0 :ran 7}
   :web {:exit 0 :ran 7}
   :typed-abi-descriptors ["bool" "i64" "keyword" ["option" "i64"]]}
  :two-module
  {:shape "optlib exports `pick` (called on both arms) AND `unreached` (an option-returning fn main never calls); optapp calls only pick"
   :command "node bin/amu compile optapp.kotoba --source-path <dir> --unpinned --target <t> --output <o>"
   :wasm32 {:exit 0 :ran 907}
   :wasm32-browser {:exit 0 :ran 907}
   :web {:exit 0 :ran 907}
   :note "907 = 7 from the some arm + 900 from the else of the none arm, so neither arm is collapsed. This is the half that mattered: the project-poisoning shape no longer reproduces."}
  :ran-through "runtime/browser-host.mjs, instantiateKotoba, instance.exports.main()"}

 :what-the-error-string-was-not
 {:searched "the literal `unsupported typed Wasm expression` across amu"
  :found "only docs/adr/0290 and a prose note in the conformance pilot manifest -- no live emit site reachable by this shape"
  :reading "the lowering gap that ADR 0290 names for map-new is a different operation; the option path had already been qualified by the time of this measurement"}

 :why-a-closed-gap-still-cost-something
 "The recorded refusal was correct when it was written. What outlived it was
  the SECOND-ORDER damage the note itself names: because ONE unreachable
  function could refuse a whole project, the guest compat surface was written
  to avoid option returns entirely. clojure.string/index-of and last-index-of
  were absent for that reason and no other -- the index half had been answered
  since 2026-09-02. An implementation state had become a house style, and
  nothing in the tree could tell anyone it had stopped being true. That is the
  defect this ADR is really about; the compiler was fine."

 :the-guard
 {:case :option-return-kit
  :entry "resources/kotoba/lang-conformance/values/option_return_kit.kotoba"
  :required-backends #{:kir :wasm32-kotoba-v1}
  :kind :run
  :expect 907
  :why-not-if-some-kit
  "if_some_kit and if_some_string_kit build an option inline and consume it in
   the same expression, so the option never crosses a function boundary and the
   RETURN-position lowering is never exercised. That is why the pilot could not
   have caught this either way -- neither its regression nor its repair."
  :carries-an-uncalled-function-on-purpose
  "`unreached` is never called. If the project-poisoning behaviour returns, the
   kit stops COMPILING rather than stops answering. Verified that it is not
   dead-code eliminated: a deliberate type error placed inside `unreached`
   alone refuses the module (exit 65, \"expected i64, got string\"), so the
   compiler does reach it."}

 :discrimination
 {:rule "a check that has not been seen to fail for the reason it names is not a check"
  :broken-on-purpose
  [{:what "kit's none-arm else value 900 -> 901"
    :result "9 failures; the report carries :kir {:result 908} and :wasm32-kotoba-v1 {:result 908, :raw-out \"908\"} against :expect 907"
    :proves "the kit RUNS on both backends and the value is compared -- it is not skipped, and it is not merely compiled"}
   {:what "a type error inside `unreached` only"
    :result "exit 65 at compile"
    :proves "the uncalled function is genuinely compiled, so the poison-half guard is real"}]
  :also "adding the case turned the golden-digest ratchet red on its own (:extra-live, and 63 declared vs 62 golden) before the golden was regenerated, which is the manifest ratchet doing its job"}

 :suite
 {:before "1335 tests, 9603 assertions, 0 failures"
  :after "1335 tests, 9607 assertions, 0 failures"
  :touched ["resources/kotoba/lang-conformance/pilot-manifest.edn"
            "resources/kotoba/lang-conformance/pilot-golden.edn"
            "test/kotoba/compiler/lang_conformance_test.clj (ratchet 62/57 -> 63/58)"]}

 :consequences
 ["The pilot now exercises an option in return position on wasm32, so this
   cannot regress silently again."
  "kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang lands clojure.string/index-of and last-index-of
   returning [:option :i64], and corrects lang/compat.edn, in its own PR."
  "The remaining :absent entries in that file were re-read against this
   measurement: split / split-lines / join are blocked on an element accessor
   for [:list :string], and lower-case / upper-case / capitalize on locale --
   none of them on this. They stay absent for their own reasons."]

 :rule-this-instance-of
 "Read a rule that blocks a design and ask whether it states a PROPERTY or an
  IMPLEMENTATION STATE. This one said `it refuses`, with a date and a SHA
  attached -- an implementation state, and the honest kind, which is why
  re-measuring it took one command. The failure was not that the note was
  written; it was that nothing re-ran it."}
